WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.868
-Come on. Come on.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.100
I'm so happy
you guys are all here.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.801
-We're happy to be here.

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.634
-But before we get into things,

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.534
I don't want to spoil
anything for people

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:10.234
who haven't watched
the finale yet.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:13.534
So if you don't want to hear
a spoiler, plug your ears now.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:16.234
Okay? No.
You guys know what happened.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:18.267
Yeah, yeah.
Mai, congratulations.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:19.667
You won "Squid Game:
The Challenge."

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.567
-Thank you so much. Yes.
-This is fantastic.

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
What does it feel like?

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:26.567
What has today -- What has today
been like for you?

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:29.634
-Liberating and I feel like...
-Is it liberating?

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:32.234
-Yes. It's like --
Because the burden

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:33.601
has just lifted off my shoulder.

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:34.968
-Because you couldn't
tell anyone what happened.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.834
-Exactly. Yeah.
-No family. Nothing.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:40.033
-Except my husband.
-Yeah, just your husband.

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.934
Explain to me
what goes into this

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:43.801
because I know "Squid Game"
comes out,

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.267
it's a giant hit on Netflix.

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:47.767
Love it. And then they go,
"We're actually going to make

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:50.601
that show into an actual
reality competition."

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.267
I go, "How is this possible?"

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:55.033
And they did it in
a fantastic way. It was so good.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:58.200
But you get the -- Do you see
an audition somewhere?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.067
Do you go, "Hey,
I want to get into this"?

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:01.601
What'd you think?
-Just saw an ad online

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.501
and applied.
-And you thought that,

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.300
"I could do what the show..."

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.834
Have you ever seen "Squid Game"?

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:09.234
-So, I'd never actually
seen the show

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.868
until after I got casted.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.067
-Is that correct?
-Yeah.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:14.501
-How about you?
Did you see the show before?

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:17.300
Did you see it?
-I saw it. I was a huge fan.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.834
Um, I clearly
don't value my life.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.200
-No, I mean --

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.701
Seriously, obviously,
no one's going to die,

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.901
but I mean, like,
they did it so well.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.934
When you watch,
you'll see how they did it.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:31.534
It was just perfectly done.
Do you go into it and go,

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:33.667
"Okay, I got to start
working on some strategies"?

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.634
Is there strategies?

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:38.501
-Um, there's no real strategy.
I mean, a lot of it is luck.

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.701
I got casted three days
before I flew out,

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:42.567
so there was basically
no time to prepare.

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:45.000
And a lot of it
was just friendships.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.367
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:50.167
-For me, it's, uh --
There's a balance of 50/50.

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.934
There's chance,
and there's strategy.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.601
And I did not prepare for it.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:56.667
But I did watch the show twice,
you know, just to get

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:59.667
the idea of the games
and the mentality of the players

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.701
on the TV show.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.634
-And what'd your husband say?
He said you should do it?

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:06.200
-Yeah, he's the one
who encouraged me to do it.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.901
-Oh, my gosh!
Did you -- I would --

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:10.501
-he apparently doesn't love me.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:12.234
-No. Yeah. He's so...

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:13.701
Well, he definitely
loves you now.

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:15.200
Okay? Yeah. Hello!

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.734
I mean, it's a lot of money,
by the way.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.033
-Yes.
-It's one of the largest

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:20.601
in the history of reality shows.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.734
$4.56 million?

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.367
-But do you know Uncle Sam?
This is not Uncle Sam.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.567
Do you know Uncle Sam?
He's gonna take half of it.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:30.667
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
It's still a good...

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.968
What are you gonna do
with the money?

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:35.367
-I want to do my cause,
you know.

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:38.534
I believe in the passion
about charity work.

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:42.033
So the three things are climate,
animals, and underprivileged.

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:44.133
And I want to expand
that horizon.

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:45.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Good for you. That's awesome.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:47.567
I mean, you're all great people.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.968
You're also -- You're in a band.

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:52.200
-Yes. Uh, my new band,
Six Ways to Saturday.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.701
We just dropped a single today.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.334
It's called "Fantasy."
Check us out.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:56.968
-Yeah. Alright. Good.
It's out today?

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.033
-Yeah. Out today.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:01.734
-And I can't help but notice,
but you have a beautiful beard.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:04.400
You're going into the beard
kind of business.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.667
-Yes, yeah,
I have a gender-inclusive

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:09.667
beard-care brand, uh,
caring for facial hair,

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.834
that anybody can --
anybody can grow facial hair.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:15.300
They don't have to identify
as, you know, a man.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.467
And a lot of the beard-care
brands out there

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.534
right now are just --

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:22.567
kind of narrow focus
to, you know, a Viking,

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:24.868
you're a lumberjack,
you're a warrior.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:27.734
And, you know,
beards are beautiful.

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:29.200
Beards make you beautiful.
-Yeah.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.934
That's fantastic. Very good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:33.834
-It makes you want to grow
a beard now, right?

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:35.901
-It does. Yeah.
I wanted to ask you --

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:38.367
Because out of all the games
that you played,

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.501
of course,
they're ones from the show.

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:41.801
The red light, green light one,

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:44.234
which was the first episode,
which was frightening.

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:47.634
And then the last game,
it was rock, paper, scissors

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.267
that you won all this money on.

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:51.100
Rock, paper, scissors.
-I know, right?

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.868
-That is how you won
all this money.

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:56.000
Out of every game you played,
that is the one I go,

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.334
"Oh, my gosh."

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:59.033
-I couldn't ask
for a better game.

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.100
-Did you know
that was going to be...

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.567
-No.
-No. No one knows that.

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:04.868
But do you have a strategy when
it goes to rock paper, scissors?

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.734
-Well, I have a concept
of just playing

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:09.334
throughout my childhood
and my adult life.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:13.100
And so I have a statistic

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.934
of what men would do, women
would do, or kids would do.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.167
-But you knew this
going into "Squid Game"?

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:19.567
-Yes, yes.
-And what is the --

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:21.901
-And I also --
You know, I'm older than him,

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:24.300
so I have an advantage...
[ Laughs ]

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.501
...of experience in life.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.167
-Like, right now
if I played you,

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.968
do you think
that you could beat me?

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.567
-Yes. Of course I could.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:31.968
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:34.067
[ Laughs ]

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:36.000
-Do you want me
to know your strategy?

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.868
-You already know my strategy,

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:39.667
but I'm gonna
modify that strategy.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.267
-Alright.
So what is the strategy?

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:43.467
-I'm not gonna tell you.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:45.300
-Okay. You ready for this?
-Yeah.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.567
-You ready for this?!
Rock, paper, scissors! Yeah.

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:50.634
This is the "Squid Game:
The Challenge" super champion.

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:51.968
Ready?
-Okay.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:53.601
-So how do we go?
One, two, three, right?

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:55.734
-One, two, three, go!

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:58.667
-Aah!
-Ohh!

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:01.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.701
I'm so happy you won.
Congratulations.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.601
You guys were all
great contestants.

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:07.534
-Thank you.
-You were all great contestants.

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:09.067
Congratulations again.
-Thank you.

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:10.601
-That was fun.
The finalists from

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.567
"Squid Game: The Challenge,"
everybody.

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:14.767
All episodes of
"Squid Game: The Challenge"

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:16.701
are streaming now on Netflix.

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:19.634
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show." Come on back.

